berger's story not widely  known today  for one thing fairy porsche himself  played a big part in erasing the jewish  co-founder from the company's history  almost a decade after rosenberger's  death ferry published his first  autobiography titled we at porsche  in it he twisted the truth around what  happened to rosenberger as well as other  german jews who were forced to sell  their businesses and flee the nazis  ferry who was also a former ss officer  peppered his account with anti-semitic  stereotypes and claimed it was the  porsche family who had saved rosenberger  from the concentration camp the perverse  irony ends up that  a  former ss officer  ends up introducing the porsche car in  america and not  the persecuted jewish co-founder of  porsche who has immigrated to america  that is yet another incredible tragedy  of the tale of rosenberger's life  in porsha's second autobiography  published in the 1980s ferry changed his  story removing the anti-semitism from  the narrative and reducing the story of  rosenberger to just two paragraphs  but he continued to deny arianization  took place and porsha's corporate  position has also largely been quiet on  this part of the company's history  and today you have the very porsche  foundation  which  you know is sponsoring  professorship in corporate history even  though the porsche family has never  spoken about very porsche's anti-semitic  statements about ferry porsche's  voluntary application to the 2dss and  very porsche populating the porsche  company in the 1950s and 60s as ceo with  former high-ranking ss officers  so  what is happening is that  there is a  global foundation today in the name of  ferry porsche  which perversely is pretending to be  engaged within history but nothing could  be farther from the truth  it was not until 2019 when the german  public finally got to learn about adolf  rosenberger's founding role at porsche  a public television documentary  chronicled his saga as a company  co-founder 